open the .env file and enter your api key before running

remember to remove the .example extension from the .env file or create a new .env file and paste your api key there. You can generate or find new api keys from google ai studio

to run run the following command: python scanner.py Vulnerable.py

Also before I forget you might encounter issues with the model I chose so please feel free to change the ai model to the one that is available to you at the time

